      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-mono leading-relaxed">

<p class="mb-4">If you're looking for the best matcha latte near Platja d'Aro, the most specific answer we can give you is this: Dirty Rabbit in S'Agaró, ten minutes away. We opened on 1 November 2024 with a menu built around named suppliers.</p>
<p class="mb-4">But "the best" is a claim that needs backing up, not just stating. So here's what we do and why we think it matters.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What makes a good matcha latte</h3>
<ol class="list-decimal list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>The supplier. We use REQ Matcha — a Barcelona project with a Japanese founder who lives in Japan and selects the tea directly at the plantations. That's why the colour is deep green, the flavour is clean, and there's none of the bitterness that many people associate with matcha because they've only tried low-quality versions.</li>
  <li>The dose. 2g of ceremonial matcha per cup is the industry standard for a balanced cup. Want it stronger? There's an extra strong option for a little more. There's no watered-down version that looks the same in the glass but tastes like nothing.</li>
  <li>Technique. We whisk it cold with water first, then add the milk. That's the step most places skip because it slows things down. It's also the step that determines whether the cup is smooth or has clumped powder at the bottom.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What matcha you can order</h3>
<ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>Classic matcha latte — hot or iced, with plant milk available</li>
  <li>Orange matcha — with orange juice instead of milk (dairy-free, more refreshing)</li>
  <li>Extra strong — higher dose, for a little more</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Where to find the best matcha latte near Platja d'Aro</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Dirty Rabbit, Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275, S'Agaró — about ten minutes from central Platja d'Aro.</p>
<p class="mb-4">In Platja d'Aro centre there are options to sit on the promenade or near the beach. If the matcha itself is the point — not the setting — the detour to S'Agaró is worth it. Large terrace, good morning light, WiFi. Easy parking right across the road.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Matcha is available year-round, hot or cold, with dairy or plant milk. Iwonka runs the day-to-day with a simple rule: if she can't explain where an ingredient comes from, it doesn't go on the menu.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Why matcha is everywhere but good matcha is rare</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Platja d'Aro is a high-volume tourist destination. That pushes many local businesses towards low-cost, high-availability suppliers. Japanese ceremonial matcha doesn't fit that category — it's more expensive, has more potential failure points in preparation, and requires staff who understand why it matters.</p>
<p class="mb-4">The result is that quality matcha in the Platja d'Aro area is scarce. Not non-existent, but scarce. The places doing it well are the ones that made deliberate choices about which ingredients they wanted to work with, regardless of margin.</p>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
