<div class="space-y-6">
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Where is the best matcha latte near Platja d'Aro?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Dirty Rabbit in S'Agaró, Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275. Ten minutes by car from central Platja d'Aro. Organic ceremonial matcha from REQ Matcha, standard dose 2g with an extra strong option available.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">What's the difference between a regular matcha latte and a ceremonial one?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Ceremonial matcha is made from the youngest green tea leaves, stone-ground. The flavour is smoother, the green is more intense, and there's no bitterness from generic powder. The difference is noticeable from the first sip if you've tried both.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">How much does a matcha latte cost at Dirty Rabbit?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Between €3.50 and €5. Quality matcha has a higher ingredient cost — the price reflects that.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Do you have dairy-free options?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes. We work with dairy milk and plant-based alternatives. Ask at the counter what's available that day.</p>
</div>
